==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{L.}} ''[[bona#Latin|bonā]] [[fide]]'' ("in good faith") which is the {{abl}} of ''[[bona#Latin|bona]] [[fides]]'' ("good faith"). Literally meaning "in good faith".

===Pronunciation===
* {{italbrac|[[RP]]}} {{IPA|/ˌbəʊnəˈfaɪdi/ ''or'' /ˌbəʊnəˈfaɪdeɪ/}}
* {{italbrac|US}} {{IPA|/ˈboʊnə.faɪd/ ''or'' /ˈboʊnəˌfiːdeɪ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-bona-fide_2.ogg|Audio (US)}}, {{audio|en-us-bona-fide.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Done in [[good]] [[faith]].
#: ''Although he failed, the prime minister made a '''bona fide''' attempt to repair the nation's damaged economy.''
# [[genuine|Genuine]]; not [[counterfeit]].
#: ''This is a '''bona fide''' Roman coin.''
#* '''2000''': ''[http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0190590/quotes O Brother Where Art Thou?]'' (movie),
#*: Ulysses Everett McGill: I am the only daddy you got! I'm the damn paterfamilias!
#*: Wharvey Gal: But you ain't '''bona fide'''!

====Synonyms====
* {{italbrac|done in good faith}}: [[sincere]]
